    1. Choose lattice dimensions R=2, C=3 and block size BH=3, BW=2
    2. Pick bg=0. Choose 6 non-bg colors for the output interior (repeats allowed)
    3. Build the output grid with bg border and interior majority colors
    4. For each block, fill BH x BW cells with its majority color
    5. For each block, replace 0-2 cells with a random non-bg minority color (different from majority); ensure majority remains strictly dominant
    6. Assemble input by interleaving blocks with 1-wide bg separator rows/cols and bg border
