<description>
Complete partial workspace sprites by matching them to full templates shown in the non-black catalog region.

Input structure
- A large non-black connected region is the catalog background.
- Multi-color template sprites touch that catalog background; all other
  foreground objects lie in the black workspace.
- Some workspace objects are partial views of a catalog template, while
  distractor objects do not match any template part.

Rule
- For each workspace object, find the unique catalog template that it matches:
  either a full template bbox filled with one template border color, a
  uniquely sized single-color mask of the template, or a multi-color boundary
  window of the template.
- Stamp the full matched template at the aligned position, treating catalog
  background cells inside the template bbox as transparent.
- Leave workspace objects with no template match unchanged.

Key insight
- The colored objects in the catalog are not to be copied in order; they are
  a legend of target sprites, and each incomplete workspace object determines
  its template and alignment from the visible sub-sprite it already contains.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "workspace foreground object s outside the catalog",
  "dst": "catalog template sprite d touching the catalog background",
  "match_cond": "s equals a distinctive color mask, an edge-color filled bbox, or a multicolor boundary window of d",
  "transform": "stamp the full d at the aligned offset, treating catalog-background cells inside d.bbox as transparent; leave unmatched objects unchanged",
  "symbol_instructions": "large non-black catalog region lists the full target sprites used as templates"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 30x30 fixed
  catalog:
    shape: rectangular strip along one grid edge (top/bottom/left), thickness 6-8
    color: single non-black color (always 3 in eval [observed]), fills strip except template cutouts
    must be the largest 4-connected single-color component
  templates:
    count: 2-3, embedded inside catalog strip, 8-adjacent to catalog background
    size: 2x2 to 5x5; each template has exactly 2 colors
    structure: frame-and-fill (border color wraps interior color) or patterned; always 180-degree rotationally symmetric [observed]
    border_color: at least one color touches the sprite bbox boundary
    constraint: if two templates share the same bbox shape, their border colors must be disjoint
  workspace:
    region: the black area outside the catalog strip
    matched_objects: 2-5 solid-filled rectangles, each same bbox shape as a template, filled with that template's border color; solver stamps the full template at aligned position
    distractors: 7-11 solid-filled rectangles of 1x1 to 3x3; use template colors, catalog color, or novel colors; must NOT match any template (wrong size or wrong border color)
    total_objects: 11-16
    spacing: objects >=2 apart (Chebyshev); stamps may overlap distractors in output
  output: input with each matched object replaced by the full template sprite at aligned position; distractors unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose catalog edge (top/bottom/left), thickness 6-8, catalog color != 0
    2. Design 2-3 templates (2-color, 2x2-5x5, 180-rot-symmetric); ensure no two same-shape templates share a border color
    3. Embed templates in catalog strip surrounded by catalog color
    4. Build output workspace: place 2-5 full template stamps on black region, non-overlapping with catalog, fitting within grid
    5. Scatter 7-11 solid-filled rectangle distractors (1x1-3x3) in remaining black space; each must fail the match condition (wrong size or non-border color for that size)
    6. Derive input: replace each stamped template with a solid rectangle of the border color (same bbox), erasing interior detail
```
