0049:     Extract the color of each noisy block in a row/column lattice and mirror the coarse grid horizontally.
0050: 
0051:     Input structure:
0052:     - A background surrounds a rectangular lattice of monochrome foreground blocks.
0053:     - Consecutive rows in a lattice band share the same set of visible foreground colors.
0054:     - Consecutive columns in a lattice band share the same set of visible foreground colors.
0055:     - Each row-band/column-band intersection has one foreground color, with possible background holes.
0056: 
0057:     Rule:
0058:     - Group non-empty rows and columns into consecutive bands by their foreground color sets.
0059:     - Replace each lattice cell by the single foreground color inside that row/column-band intersection.
0060:     - Return the resulting coarse color grid with the column order reversed.
0061: 
0062:     Key insight:
0063:     - Whole-row and whole-column color sets reveal the hidden lattice even when neighboring cells share a color or contain holes.
